/public/build
# The build artifacts themselves ship out-of-band (too large for GitHub's
# push limit — see the .gitignore rules in wavebreak-mobile and
# wavebreak-pc for the same reasoning) — excluded by extension, not the
# whole directory, since version.json in this same folder is a small,
# git-tracked file the web team edits directly each time a build ships
# (see wavebreak-mobile/lib/services/update/update_service.dart) and a
# directory-level ignore would silently exclude that too (git can't
# un-ignore a file whose parent directory is itself ignored).
/public/downloads/*.apk
/public/downloads/*.exe
/public/downloads/*.zip
/public/fonts-manifest.dev.json
/public/hot
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor
_ide_helper.php
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
